<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 7th Grade (CEFR: A2.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Arts and Crafts</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> This Is a Local Artist.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write emails, letters, or texts describing past events. Interactive: Write a class project proposal with guidance.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a letter describing a visit to a local artist (e.g., "Yesterday, we visited an artist who makes molas"). Can write brief messages about past art or craft events (e.g., "Last week, our class made baskets"). Can draft a proposal for a project on local art with support (e.g., "We want to study Guna Yala art").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of key concepts and language for the writing task.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of different local crafts and artists (e.g., a Guna woman making a mola, an artist carving a tagua, baskets from Emberá communities). Students briefly review the vocabulary by identifying the crafts. T: "What crafts do you see? What did we learn about these artists?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the writing of simple descriptive sentences using target vocabulary and past simple tense. T writes on the board: "Yesterday, we visited an artist. She created a beautiful mola. Her studio was colorful." T emphasizes inflectional endings (-ed in "visited," "created") and syllable stress in words like "sculpture" or "design" as they might appear in future writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">T: "Are we writing about things happening now or in the past?" (Expected answer: "In the past.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">T: "Do we use words like 'create' or 'created' for past events?" (Expected answer: "Created.")</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to the Scenario: "Arts and Crafts". This stage provides a model for the writing task.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short email or a blog post excerpt (authentic text) describing a visit to a local artist's gallery or studio, focusing on their creations and achievements. The text includes examples of present perfect, past simple, and descriptive adjectives.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">*Example Text Snippet:*</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"Dear Class,</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Yesterday, our class visited a local artist named Elena. She has created many beautiful sculptures from recycled materials. Her gallery was a colorful building downtown. We saw a vibrant mural on one wall. She explained, 'First, you prepare the materials, then you design the shape.' It was a unique experience!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Describing creations and achievements of artists using present perfect and past simple. (Pragmatic: "This artist has created beautiful sculptures.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the text individually.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "Who did the class visit? Where did they go?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "The artist creates paintings. (False) Her gallery was small. (False)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Match words from the text (e.g., 'sculptures,' 'gallery,' 'mural') with definitions or images.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing, integrating target grammar and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences using present perfect, past simple, and imperatives. Vocabulary: artist, craft, basket, sculpture, gallery, studio, exhibition, canvas, building, mural, mola, tagua carving; create, paint, sculpt, design, carve, display; creative, artistic, handmade, colorful, abstract, bold, vibrant, minimalist, timeless, unique, detailed.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Gap-fill):</b> Students complete sentences about various art and craft events using the correct form of verbs (past simple, present perfect) and vocabulary words from a provided list.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "Last month, the artist ____ (create) a new ____ (sculpture) for the ____ (gallery)."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "Our class ____ (make) ____ (baskets) last week. First, you ____ (prepare) the materials."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Expansion):</b> The teacher provides simple sentences (e.g., "The artist painted.") and students expand them using descriptive adjectives and adverbs.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "The artist painted." → "The (creative) artist (skillfully) painted a (colorful) mural."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "She made a craft." → "She has made a (unique) craft (from) local materials."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Sentence Construction:</b> In pairs, students receive three picture prompts of different local crafts (e.g., a mola, a tagua carving, a basket). For each picture, they collaboratively write two sentences describing a past event related to it or the artist, focusing on using one past simple and one present perfect sentence. They check each other's grammar and vocabulary usage.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic writing scenario. Focus on fluency and task completion.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Written Product (Draft of a Project Proposal)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students) to draft a short proposal for a class project on local art. They use the learned vocabulary and grammar to outline their project idea, describing what they have already learned or done (present perfect) and what they plan to do (imperatives for steps). Each group will aim for a paragraph of 5-7 sentences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Instructions:</b> "Imagine our class wants to do a project on Panamanian art. As a group, draft a short proposal (a paragraph of 5-7 sentences) to present to the teacher. Include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What type of local art you want to study (e.g., Guna Yala art, Emberá crafts).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What you have learned or done about it so far (using Present Perfect).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One or two steps you propose for the project (using Imperatives, e.g., 'First, find information...').</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example sentence starters: "We want to study Guna Yala art. Our class has already learned about molas. First, we will research local artists."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> Directly aligns with drafting a proposal for a project on local art, as specified in the learning outcome.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Clear, descriptive writing, correct application of present perfect and imperatives, and appropriate vocabulary use within a collaborative project context (Sociolinguistic: Propose and develop steps for art projects).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment of student writing, followed by self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their group project proposals with another group. Each group reads and provides feedback on the other's proposal using a simple checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Does the proposal clearly state the art project idea? (Clarity)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are at least two target vocabulary words (e.g., 'artist', 'mola', 'sculpture') used correctly? (Use of target vocabulary)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are past events described using Past Simple or Present Perfect (e.g., "We have learned...")? (Grammar accuracy)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are there clear steps proposed using imperatives? (Grammar accuracy)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the message easy to understand? (Clarity)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts individually:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I wrote well today was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I want to improve in my writing is..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Learner and teacher reflection on the lesson and connection to future learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do I feel writing about past art events or describing art projects?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's writing activities did I find most helpful?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., students effectively used present perfect to describe past achievements).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson or future writing tasks? (e.g., provide more sentence starters for imperatives, focus on sentence connectors).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will use their cumulative knowledge of local artists and crafts to consolidate information and present their final project, possibly presenting the refined project proposal drafted in this lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>